"""110 complete ambush/rescue speeches andtwo separately typed choices."""
DATA={
5:('V','The reporter warns that a suspicious fleet is approaching them.',"Admiral! A suspicious fleet is heading toward us!",'Restore approach and suspicion, without naming the still-unidentified fleet or assigning the generic reporter a new rank.'),
9:('R','Lil orders the reporter to identify the fleet affiliation.',"Check who they are!",'Retain the natural concise order in the full incoming-fleet exchange; no unspoken faction identity is supplied.'),
13:('R','The reporter identifies the apparent Li family fleet, counts five ships and reports firing.',"The Li family... Admiral! They have five ships and they're firing!",'Retain the complete natural report and explicit source five-ship count. This is the reporter apparent identification, later exposed as false, not an editorial assertion of Li ownership.'),
25:('R','Gerhard echoes the Li family identification in shock.',"Li family?!",'Retain the natural startled name echo and punctuation; it does not make the deceptive identification independently true.'),
40:('R','Fernando reacts in disbelief and confusion.',"What?! That's absurd!",'Retain the natural short reaction and force. No specific hidden explanation is invented before the rescue reveal.'),
47:('R','The reporter urgently asks the admiral what to do.',"Admiral! Your orders?!",'Retain the natural nautical question and source admiral address, without giving the reporter a new title.'),
63:('R','The reporter acknowledges the fight decision and says they will engage.',"Aye! We'll engage!",'Retain the natural acknowledgement and engagement intention in the selected source path; it is not an offline-test battle victory.'),
68:('R','In the withdrawal path, the reporter says they cannot shake off the fleet.',"Admiral! We can't shake them!",'Retain the natural escape idiom and failure report. Keep this conditional path separate from choosing engagement directly.'),
71:('V','Lil realizes they must fight and wonders in disbelief whether Maria Huamei Li was an enemy.',"Ugh... We'll have to fight! Maria Huamei Li... You were an enemy? I can't believe it...",'Preserve forced-combat resolve and her shocked question about Maria, rather than treating the disguised fleet as actual proof of Maria hostility.'),
75:('R','Lil orders everyone to battle stations.',"Battle stations, everyone!",'Retain the complete natural order and collective address; no additional ship count or weapon is added.'),
79:('R','The reporter doubts whether they can beat such a fleet.',"Can we beat that fleet...?",'Retain the natural uncertain question without guaranteeing defeat or an actual tested outcome.'),
83:('V','If escape is impossible, Lil resolves to break through head-on because there is no other choice.',"If we can't shake them, we'll break through head-on! We have no choice!",'Restore the conditional setup, frontal breakthrough and explicit necessity, keeping her tactical intention distinct from an achieved escape.'),
97:('V','Fernando says luck is now decisive and trails off hoping it will favor them.',"Now it's down to luck! If luck's on our side...",'Restore the source conditional hope rather than the older generic Come on. No RNG or outcome is forced.'),
104:('V','The reporter urgently announces that more forces have appeared.',"Admiral! Trouble! More ships have appeared!",'Restore the alarm and appearance of new forces without adding an unspoken number or prematurely labeling an allied rescue force.'),
116:('R','Gerhard is astonished by the additional force.',"What?! More ships?!",'Retain the natural startled echo within the same fleet context; it does not add another distinct counted fleet.'),
123:('V','Lil reacts with a wordless exclamation.',"!",'Preserve the punctuation-only reaction and original speaker, converting the legacy full-width exclamation to supported ASCII.'),
127:('V','Facing such a huge fleet, Lil tentatively thinks even she may not stand a chance.',"A fleet that huge... Even I might not stand a chance...",'Restore personal even I and uncertainty instead of the old collective survival question; do not guarantee her death.'),
138:('V','Christina thinks they may have to steel themselves for the worst.',"It looks like we'll have to brace for the worst...",'Restore the source seems qualification and resigned courage rather than an unqualified compulsory fate.'),
153:('V','Yukihisa personally pledges to risk his life to protect FI in particular.',"{MACRO:FI}! I, Yukihisa, will risk my life to protect you!",'Preserve his emphatic self-naming and formal warrior voice, direct focus on FI and risk to his own life. The older guaranteed safety and life-is-yours ownership are not stated by the source; no group safety or successful rescue is promised by the translation.'),
160:('V','Lil regrets that she wanted to see Camille again and apologize, then says she is sorry.',"Camille... I wanted to see you again... I wanted to apologize... I'm sorry...",'Restore approved Camille, personal I and the specific wish to apologize. Do not turn the wish into romance, a mutual we or an unspoken last-ever meeting.'),
172:('R','Fernando sharply tells her not to give up so easily.',"You fool! Don't give up so easily!",'Retain the natural rough encouragement and urgency. The source blunt address does not need extra profanity or a new insult.'),
178:('V','An offscreen voice calls FI in a source-unlabeled FE panel.',"{MACRO:FI}!",'Preserve the exact name substitution and ASCII exclamation. Do not add a Camille label before the source reveals who is calling; FE is not actor254.'),
182:('R','Lil is startled and recognizes the voice.',"What?! That voice...!",'Retain the natural broken recognition without supplying the caller name early.'),
194:('R','Fernando reacts incredulously to the unexpected voice.',"No way?!",'Retain the natural brief disbelief and separate conditional companion reaction.'),
201:('V','Camille calls FI again after his source appearance.',"{MACRO:FI}!",'Preserve this separate actor9 call and exact macro while converting the old full-width punctuation. Do not merge it with the preceding FE voice.'),
214:('R','Emilio joyfully reacts to Camille return.',"Wow! He's back!",'Retain the natural delighted reaction in its separate companion alternative; no rank or relationship is added.'),
221:('V','Lil repeatedly recognizes Camille and asks if it is really him.',"Camille! Is it really you?!",'Restore approved Camille and a natural complete recognition question without an invented impostor plot.'),
232:('V','Maria tells Camille they managed to arrive in time.',"We made it in time, Camille.",'Restore approved Camille and a natural complete arrival remark. It remains dialogue in this source path, not a claimed selected-scene visit.'),
236:('R','Camille says their timely arrival was thanks to Maria and Hodram.',"Yes. Thanks to you and Hodram.",'Retain the natural grateful answer and both credited people. Mentioning Hodram does not require him to be physically present in every branch.'),
239:('R','Lil is surprised by Maria presence and asks what is happening.',"What?! Maria...? What's going on?",'Retain the complete natural confusion and approved name; no additional rank is invented from san.'),
244:('V','In the other arrival path, Hodram tells Camille they made it in time.',"We made it in time, Camille.",'Preserve the separate Hodram-present alternative with approved Camille; similar source meaning permits the same brief English without merging speakers.'),
248:('R','Maria says they arrived by the narrowest margin.',"Barely!",'Retain the natural idiomatic answer to the preceding arrival remark.'),
258:('R','If Lil does not know Hodram, she asks who he is and why Maria is there.',"Who are you? And Maria...? What's going on?",'Retain the natural confused questions. Source27 acquaintance state remains exact, so do not insert Hodram name here.'),
264:('R','In the acquainted path, Lil recognizes Hodram as an officer and wonders why he and Maria are present.',"Wait, you're Hodram, the officer! And Maria...? What's going on?",'Retain the natural complete recognition and source officer identity. Do not add Joakim, Admiral or another rank to this utterance.'),
274:('V','Camille reveals that the hostile fleets are all Kuhn disguised forces and that Kuhn planned to claim the Li family killed FI.',"Those fleets are all Kuhn's, in disguise! He was going to claim the Li family had killed {MACRO:FI}...",'Preserve the false-flag reveal, every hostile fleet and planned fabricated death. The source plan is not an achieved death or new attribution of hostility to Maria.'),
277:('V','He says this was to create a pretext for avenging the ally.',"He wanted a pretext for avenging his ally!",'Restore a natural complete explanation of the bogus vengeance motive, connected to the preceding planned false death rather than genuine mourning.'),
288:('R','Fernando curses and realizes what the scheme was.',"Damn! So that's his game!",'Retain the natural rough realization and source-level curse. It does not add a new plot beyond the just-revealed scheme.'),
295:('V','Maria identifies this as the true Kuhn and expects Lil to understand now.',"That's the real Kuhn... Do you understand now?",'Preserve her expectation as a direct question rather than declaring Lil internal realization for her.'),
298:('V','Lil personally blames herself for being foolish and repeatedly apologizes to Camille.',"I... I was such a fool... I'm sorry, Camille... I'm so sorry...",'Restore personal I, approved Camille and the repeated apology. Do not invent a demand for forgiveness or distribute her responsibility to we.'),
301:('V','Camille says talking must wait because they need to defeat Kuhn fleet.',"We can talk later! We have to defeat Kuhn's fleet!",'Preserve urgent priorities and explicit Kuhn ownership, with no claim that the battle has already been won.'),
312:('R','Gerhard agrees with Camille and addresses FI.',"Camille is right, {MACRO:FI}!",'Retain the complete natural agreement, approved Camille and exact runtime address; dono does not create a new title.'),
326:('R','Ian resolves to scatter the hostile force.',"We'll crush them!",'Retain the natural forceful combat resolve. Crush is an idiom for routing the fleet, not a newly specified physical injury or actual tested victory.'),
333:('R','Lil hesitantly agrees and regains resolve.',"Y-yes...!",'Retain the natural stammer and emphatic assent as its own beat.'),
337:('R','Kuhn panics, calls Georg and asks why Maria and especially Marinus are here.',"What's this?! Georg! Why is Maria here? And Marinus, of all people...!",'Retain the natural panicked questions and both unexpected people. Punctuation conveys the broken start without adding a new ship count or catalog name.'),
341:('R','Georg acknowledges both miscalculations and advises temporary withdrawal.',"Hmm... Neither was expected. We should withdraw for now.",'Retain the natural composed, deferential recommendation. Neither refers to the two people just named, not two invented fleets.'),
345:('V','Kuhn orders all ships to retreat and vows to repay the setback someday.',"Yes. All ships, retreat! Tch... I'll get you back for this someday!",'Restore acknowledgement, contempt and his personal future revenge intention. This is a threat, not a literal financial debt or achieved counterattack.'),
348:('V','Maria judges that they seem to have escaped the immediate crisis.',"It looks like we're out of danger.",'Restore the source appearance qualifier; the following warning still allows Kuhn to remain dangerous in the future.'),
352:('R','Lil thanks Maria, admits her earlier warning was true and apologizes for not believing her.',"Thank you... You were right. Sorry for doubting you.",'Retain the natural complete acknowledgement and personal apology; the full preceding warning supplies the earlier time reference.'),
356:('R','Maria accepts and redirects the apology toward Camille.',"That's fine. You want to apologize to him, right?",'Retain the natural gentle redirect and rhetorical question. Him is the present Camille, not a new absent relative or rival.'),
368:('V','Fernando guesses FI has a great deal she wants to say.',"{MACRO:FI}, you must have so much you want to say...",'Restore his inferred expectation and her personal wish to speak without prescribing an actual speech or a group confession.'),
381:('R','Maria gently prompts Camille by name.',"Camille.",'Retain the natural brief prompt with approved name; kun does not add a son, apprentice or formal rank.'),
387:('R','Hodram prompts Camille in the other path.',"Camille.",'Retain the matching natural prompt as a separate Hodram-present alternative, without making him Camille father.'),
395:('V','Camille hesitantly responds, apologizes to FI and starts to explain himself.',"Y-yes. {MACRO:FI}, I'm sorry... I...",'Restore the interrupted first-person start and exact macro rather than dropping his attempt to explain before Lil responds.'),
399:('V','Lil says she is the one who should apologize, addresses Camille and begins acknowledging the Kuhn relation.',"I'm the one who should apologize. I'm sorry, Camille... You're Kuhn's...",'Restore responsibility to apologize rather than an unbounded claim that every event is her fault. Keep the source cutoff and approved name before the confession.'),
403:('R','Camille explains his maternal surname, real name Marinus Kuhn and being Antony Kuhn son.',"Yes... Overijssel is Mother's surname. My real name is Marinus Kuhn. Antony Kuhn's son.",'Retain the natural formal confession and final appositive fragment. All names, maternal surname and family identity are complete; no legal procedure or new runtime nameplate is invented.'),
406:('V','Lil recalls the bartender saying Camille was a nickname and now confirms that fact.',"Come to think of it, the bartender said Camille was a nickname... So it really was.",'Restore supported ASCII and natural reflection without inventing an uncle. This recollection does not make the earlier bartender remember the actual birth name.'),
410:('V','Camille says his face was even more girlish as a child; someone began using a girl name partly as a joke.',"I had an even more girlish face as a child. Someone started calling me by a girl's name as a bit of a joke.",'Preserve his own respectful account of the nickname origin and the source partial-joke tone. Remove the stronger old teased framing; add no slur, bullying event or modern identity claim.'),
414:('R','Only his father never used the nickname because by then he was no longer his former self.',"Only my father never used it. He'd already changed by then...",'Retain the natural exception and emotional explanation. Do not invent that the father disapproved of a feminine nickname or a gender identity.'),
418:('V','His father used to be good and was reportedly a small trader when he met the mother.',"My father was a good man once. I heard he was just a small-time trader when he met Mother.",'Preserve the reported-account qualification and humble beginnings without newly assigning the source of this particular report.'),
421:('R','His mother said they had been poor but happy and each day joyful.',"Mother said they were poor, but happy. Every day was a joy.",'Retain the complete idiomatic account and explicit maternal attribution. Mother is natural familial register in this public retelling and introduces no different relative.'),
424:('V','The Kuhn Company began profiting on entering the Spice Islands, and great wealth changed the father.',"But the Kuhn Company started making money as soon as it entered the Spice Islands. Wealth changed Dad...",'Restore the actual named Spice Islands instead of generic spice-growing islands, immediate timing and personal effect of wealth.'),
428:('R','Greed blinded him; he thought only of profit and would not shrink from dirty methods.',"Greed blinded him. He cared only about profit, and would use any dirty trick...",'Retain the natural account of unscrupulous willingness. The preceding wealth-change sentence supplies the progression; any dirty trick is an idiom, not an invented list of crimes.'),
432:('V','Camille and his mother could not bear the behavior.',"Mother and I couldn't bear it.",'Restore grammatical named personal subjects and their emotional burden without inventing a specific act of domestic abuse.'),
435:('V','Lil sympathetically addresses Camille.',"Camille...",'Restore approved Camille and retain the separate listening beat.'),
439:('R','People feared the father and even neighbors avoided mother and son.',"Everyone feared him. Even our neighbors shunned Mother and me...",'Retain the natural account and inclusion of both affected family members. Shunned expresses avoidance, not an added attack or hatred motive.'),
443:('V','His mother judged they could no longer live there and took him back to the Netherlands.',"Mother thought we couldn't live there anymore. She took me back to the Netherlands.",'Restore her judgment rather than the old knew and preserve country/return without adding a city or number of years.'),
447:('V','He had not intended to tell anyone about his father and especially did not want FI to know.',"{MACRO:FI}... I wasn't going to tell anyone about my father... Especially you.",'Restore personal intention instead of the older impersonal nobody-was-meant-to-know, preserving the particular reluctance toward Lil.'),
450:('V','He refers to his conduct at the earlier time and apologizes.',"That's why I acted that way back then... I'm sorry.",'Restore the backward reference and natural apology while leaving the precise act unspecified, as in the source.'),
453:('R','Lil quietly acknowledges the explanation.',"Yes...",'Retain the natural subdued response without claiming a new guarantee or deleting the emotional pause.'),
465:('R','Fernando realizes what had been behind the earlier behavior.',"So that's what it was...",'Retain the natural retrospective realization; it adds no new private knowledge beyond the confession everyone just heard.'),
472:('V','Camille asks FI to let him sail aboard her ship again.',"{MACRO:FI}... Will you let me aboard your ship again...?",'Restore direct personal vulnerability and her agency rather than the older third-person old-shipmate flourish. No new recruitment contract is introduced.'),
475:('R','Lil says of course, questions why he asks, and says his absence was very hard.',"Of course! What are you saying? Things were so hard without you!",'Retain the natural emphatic welcome and worried familiarity; it is reassurance between companions, not an invented romance.'),
479:('R','Camille gratefully thanks FI.',"{MACRO:FI}... Thank you!",'Retain the natural broken gratitude and exact runtime name.'),
482:('R','Lil teasingly says he must repay the worry he caused by working hard.',"You worried me sick! Repay me by working hard!",'Retain the natural worried-me-sick idiom and playful repayment demand after his welcome. It is neither a medical diagnosis nor a financial/labor contract.'),
485:('R','Camille sighs that she still works people hard.',"Whew... Still a hard taskmaster!",'Retain the natural wry sigh and figurative complaint in the reunion banter. Taskmaster is descriptive teasing, not an invented formal rank.'),
488:('R','Lil privately feels relief that Camille has returned.',"(Camille's back... What a relief.)",'Retain the already natural approved name and inner thought parentheses; this is not a newly spoken confession.'),
498:('R','Maria asks whether the misunderstanding is resolved.',"All cleared up now?",'Retain the natural question whose referent is the just-discussed misunderstanding, not the entire unfinished route.'),
502:('R','Camille thanks Maria and Hodram sincerely.',"Yes. You and Hodram have my heartfelt thanks.",'Retain the natural respectful gratitude and both credited helpers; mentioning Hodram does not force his physical presence in the absent variant.'),
506:('R','Hodram asks whether they have reconciled.',"Made up yet?",'Retain the natural colloquial question about the companions misunderstanding, without inventing a romantic relationship.'),
510:('V','Camille acknowledges that Hodram also made this possible.',"Hodram... This is thanks to you, too.",'Restore also instead of the older all-thanks-to-you, which could erase Maria contribution.'),
513:('V','Hodram jokes that Maria tricked him and merely told him to bring Camille here aboard his ship, claiming he did nothing.',"Maria tricked me. She just told me to bring Camille here aboard my ship. I didn't do a thing.",'Restore approved Camille and the explicit self-effacing denial that sets up Maria retort. This is dry character banter, not a narrator finding he had no role.'),
517:('R','Maria challenges his tricked claim because he had understood what was happening.',"Tricked? You knew all along!",'Retain the natural incredulous echo and teasing response. This is her characterization of his understanding, not an independent grant of omniscience.'),
520:('V','Camille thanks Maria for notifying him of the attack.',"Maria... Thank you for telling me about the attack!",'Restore the informed recipient to Camille. The old us could imply Lil and her company were warned before the ambush, contradicting their shock and the whole rescue exchange.'),
527:('R','Maria accepts, expects repayment of the favor someday and says they will leave.',"You're welcome. Repay this favor someday. Time for us to go.",'Retain the natural favor banter, indefinite someday and departure. No amount, literal financial contract or earned voyage is added.'),
531:('R','She warns that a setback of this scale will not finish Kuhn and tells them to prepare.',"Be warned: a setback won't stop Kuhn. Be ready for what comes next.",'Retain the natural concise warning and future preparation without supplying an unspoken next attack or guaranteed result.'),
535:('R','Camille agrees his father will not give up so easily and finds the future even more frightening.',"Yes. My father won't give up. What comes next scares me even more.",'Retain the natural personal assessment and increased fear. These remain his expectations, not a played future confrontation.'),
539:('R','Maria agrees with his assessment.',"True.",'Retain the natural brief agreement in the full conversation, without turning it into an external narrator guarantee.'),
549:('V','Maria expects Camille and FI to overcome what comes if he lends her his strength.',"But Camille, if you help {MACRO:FI}, I'm sure you'll get through this together.",'Restore approved Camille, conditional cooperation and her confident expectation without inventing a new guaranteed actual outcome.'),
553:('V','Camille says he will try hard, thanks her and asks her to relay a message to Hodram.',"Yes... I'll do my best. Thank you so much. Please tell Hodram...",'Restore an effort commitment rather than the older Count on me guarantee; keep Hodram absent-recipient message framing distinct from the present branch.'),
557:('V','He asks her to thank Hodram for introducing him to Maria and helping him recover his footing.',"Thank him for introducing me to you and helping me get back on my feet...",'Restore the specific introduction participants instead of ambiguous us. Get back on my feet expresses emotional recovery, not an invented healed physical injury.'),
560:('V','He also asks Hodram not to give up pursuing the strongest fleet.',"And tell him not to give up on his goal of the strongest fleet.",'Keep the message addressed through Maria to Hodram; the older direct imperative could instead instruct her. This is aspiration, not an achieved rank or fleet.'),
563:('R','Maria agrees to relay the message.',"Will do.",'Retain the natural complete acknowledgement of the just-requested fictional message; no separate new action or deadline is invented.'),
569:('V','In person, Hodram says Camille can now overcome this, urges cooperation with FI as proof and says he will leave.',"You can get through this now, Camille. Work with {MACRO:FI} and prove it. I'll be going.",'Restore approved Camille, changed personal confidence and overcoming rather than merely facing danger. Prove it is the ordinary verb, not a new Proof artifact.'),
573:('R','Camille thanks Hodram and wishes him the strongest fleet as soon as possible.',"Thank you, Hodram. Hope your fleet becomes the strongest soon!",'Retain the natural aspirational farewell; soon is a wish, not an invented one-day deadline or achieved supremacy.'),
579:('R','Maria begins to leave, remembers something and offers it.',"Time for me to go... Oh! Take this.",'Retain the natural conversational departure and remembered-gift transition as its own source beat.'),
582:('V','Camille asks what the offered object is.',"What's this?",'Restore the clear object-identification question without naming an artifact absent from this utterance.'),
586:('V','Maria says the object is a key to solving a Proof map and gives it to their group.',"It's a key to deciphering a Proof of Supremacy map. You can have it.",'Preserve the actual offered map-solving key and full approved Proof term. Do not confuse this with her metaphorical hope or147 keys to saving Asia, or invent a specific item name.'),
591:('R','Camille gratefully thanks her for the object.',"Thank you so much!",'Retain the natural grateful response without an invented reciprocal contract.'),
595:('V','Lil asks why Maria is so good to her despite her repeated rudeness.',"Maria... Why are you so kind to me? I've been nothing but rude to you...",'Preserve her personal humility and broad rude conduct rather than narrowing it to the older remarks only. No romantic motive is supplied.'),
599:('R','Maria says she found hope in Lil.',"Because you give me hope.",'Retain the natural English expression of the hope she discovered in Lil and still has. Hope is an abstract expectation, not a named item or prophecy.'),
602:('R','Lil asks about the word hope.',"Hope?",'Retain the natural puzzled echo and source question.'),
606:('V','Maria believes Lil will save Asia and its nations divided by European powers that cannot even maintain independence.',"I'm sure you'll save Asia... Its nations are divided by Europe's great powers and can't even keep their independence.",'Preserve her confidence, colonial division and independence context as Maria political account. Do not flatten it to generic need, invent one specific European occupier or make a narrator promise of salvation.'),
609:('R','Lil doubts whether she can do something of that scale.',"Can someone like me do that...?",'Retain the natural personal self-doubt and tentative question rather than giving her an immediate guarantee.'),
612:('V','Maria reassures her, recalls the dream of making needy people worldwide happy and points to Asian people being in need now.',"You can. Your dream is to make people in need all over the world happy, right? The people of Asia need help now.",'Restore worldwide scope and the present need itself. The older need-you wording implied exclusive dependence on Lil rather than the source appeal to her stated dream.'),
615:('V','She recalls Lil claim that dreams come true and says she decided to try putting her hopes in that person.',"Besides, you're the one who said dreams come true. I thought I'd take a chance on you.",'Preserve the remembered claim and her chosen wager on Lil, without the older invented exclusivity that only Lil is worthy of faith.'),
619:('V','Lil thanks Maria and commits to try hard and do all she can.',"Maria... Thank you. I'll do my best. I'll try as hard as I can.",'Preserve gratitude and effort rather than guaranteeing she alone will save every nation or asking others to count on an achieved result.'),
623:('R','Lil expresses sincere thanks.',"Thank you for everything.",'Retain the natural sincere thanks for the rescue, trust and gift in the full exchange; no additional service or obligation is created.'),
627:('R','Camille invites her to get going.',"Come on!",'Retain the natural invitation to depart in context, not an accusation of disbelief or a newly played voyage.'),
631:('R','Lil enthusiastically agrees.',"Yeah!",'Retain the natural brief enthusiastic answer and her familiar voice.'),
643:('R','Jam exuberantly says the decision is made and calls for departure with a cheer.',"Then it's settled! Let's go! Yahoo!",'Retain the lively natural closing, including the source English-loan Lets go and cheer. Do not add a new regional accent, rank or actual completed departure.')}
